WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:06.870
The Riddler is one of the most famous villains
in all of comic book history, second perhaps

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.370
only to the Joker.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:13.220
Since first appearing in an October 1948 issue
of "Detective Comics," Edward E. Nygma [NIGG-mah]

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:18.150
has continuously proven to be one of Batman's
most challenging foes.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:24.350
Known for his love of crime, drama, and, of
course, one singularly puzzling punctuation

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:29.109
mark, the Riddler has appeared in nearly as
many mediums as the Batman himself.

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:33.040
In addition to his long history in the comic
books, the Riddler has also made a number

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.899
of memorable appearances in animated form.

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:40.440
Most animated Riddler fans are likely familiar
with John Glover's iteration of the character

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.449
from 1992's "Batman: The Animated Series,"
but Glover's animated version of the character

00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:47.760
is actually only one of many.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:53.670
The first animated Riddler appeared in a 1968
CBS TV series titled "The Batman/Superman

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:54.670
Hour."

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:59.369
In his first animated incarnation, the famous
villain is voiced by actor Ted Knight, and

00:00:59.369 --> 00:01:05.159
since the Riddler's debut in animation, he
has been voiced by no less than 14 different

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:06.159
actors.

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:10.420
Of course, most people are probably more familiar
with the various live-action adaptations of

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.420
the character.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.820
In the 1960s, Nygma was played by two actors.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:18.020
"The Addams Family" star John Astin played
the character in the second season of Adam

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.920
West's "Batman" TV series.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.460
However, the actor who arguably made the character
famous was Frank Gorshin, whose portrayal

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:30.749
of the character in seasons 1 and 3 of the
show is still considered one of the best versions

00:01:30.749 --> 00:01:32.630
of the character ever.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:37.170
Gorshin's Riddler was so beloved by audiences
and critics that the actor was nominated for

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.200
an Emmy, a first for the "Batman" franchise.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.530
Gorshin would also go on to reprise his role
as the Riddler in the 1966 film of the same

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.659
name, and in the years since, the Riddler's
fame has only grown.

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:52.719
Many millennials probably first came to know
the character as a result of Jim Carrey's

00:01:52.719 --> 00:01:55.509
role in 1995's "Batman Forever."

00:01:55.509 --> 00:02:01.409
Though that film isn't beloved by many, Carrey's
campy performance is often noted as a highlight

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:02.409
of the movie.

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:03.409
[Batman forever.

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:04.409
1:32:49 until 1:32:53..

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:05.479
"Now that's impressive."

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:06.749
does a thing.]

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:11.640
Modern TV audiences may be more familiar with
Cory Michael Smith's take on Nygma from the

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.870
2014 Fox series "Gotham."

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:19.450
Matt Reeves' "The Batman" is also set to tackle
a new incarnation of the infamous character.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.900
According to a recent interview with Reeves,
this version of the Riddler is actually named

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.770
Edward Nashton and is loosely based on the
Zodiac Killer.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:31.790
So, who is the next actor set to bring him
to life?

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:36.210
Emmy Award-nominated actor Paul Dano [DANE-oh]
will portray the infamous villain in Robert

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.959
Pattinson's first outing as the Caped Crusader.

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:44.540
Since Dano's casting was first announced in
October 2019, Dano has maintained the usual

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:49.520
vow of silence against spoilers, but he's
also been willing to offer a few teases about

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.489
his unique take on the character.

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:57.709
In a recent interview with Empire Magazine,
Dano called his costume "intense" and "powerful."

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:02.659
If you recognize Dano, that's because he's
been a working actor since the late 1990s.

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:07.330
In fact, Dano's relationship with Warner Bros.
goes all the way back to his first on-screen

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.299
appearance in a 1998 episode of "Smart Guy."

00:03:10.299 --> 00:03:15.239
In the early years of his career, Dano established
himself with a handful of small roles, including

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:17.540
two minor appearances on "The Sopranos."

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.410
While Dano has worked on a few television
series, including an Emmy-nomina ted role

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:25.180
on Showtime's "Escape at Dannemora" [dan-uh-MOR-uh],
the majority of the actor's work has been

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.659
on the big screen.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:31.840
Many audiences first became aware of Dano
for his role in 2006's "Little Miss Sunshine,"

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:37.469
but his portrayal of Paul and Eli Sunday in
2007's "There Will Be Blood" may have been

00:03:37.469 --> 00:03:39.469
what rocketed the young actor to the A-list.

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:45.140
For his work in the film, Dano was nominated
for a BAFTA Award for Best Supporting Actor.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:49.650
In the years since, Dano has also appeared
in movies as varied as "Prisoners," "Love

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:52.180
and Mercy," and "Swiss Army Man."

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:57.469
You can get a full look at Dano's Riddler
when "The Batman" hits theaters on March 4.

